.vscode/

# Runtime output. The pipeline writes its logs beside the config it was given
# and moves files through ./watched, so both land inside the repository during
# a local run. Neither belongs in version control: a log records the paths and
# filenames a real deployment processed, and the watched tree is whatever the
# last run happened to be fed.
*.log
logs/
config/logs/
watched/
